  "algorithm_note": "Best-label queue ordered lexicographically by (checked u128 distance, hop count, full edge ID sequence), with stale-label suppression and one best label per node. Tuple order is extension-monotone: distance adds the same nonnegative edge length; hop count adds one; equal-hop edge sequences have equal length, so appending the same edge preserves their lexicographic order. Any route revisiting a node contains a nonnegative cycle; removing it lowers distance or preserves distance while reducing hops, so simple-path filtering cannot remove the globally preferred route. Dense layered and late-tie zero-cycle unit oracles exercise this behavior.",
